[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html:16[39m:

  - A native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label class="task">[39m, so clicking the text toggles it and it's
    keyboard/screen-reader accessible for free.
  - One CSS rule strikes the label through when checked, which is the visible "done" state.

  No JS needed — the native checkbox already owns the on/off state. The item text is a placeholder; if these tasks come
  from data, say where and I'll wire the markup to it.

  No tests were run: the repo has no test setup (single static HTML file, no package manifest).

